      "nets": ["NET0100", "NET0092", "NET0014"],
      "observed": "The FCC USB-UART bridge U6 is connected to NET0092 and NET0014. On FCC2, NET0092 is PB15, but NET0014 is PD8; PB14 is on NET0100 and is not connected to U6.",
      "expected": "The schematic identifies UART1 as the debug interface and specifies the USART1 bootloader pins as PB14/PB15. The bridge should connect to both pins of the intended UART rather than PB15 and PD8.",
      "evidence": [
        {
          "source": "schematic",
          "quote": "\"UART1 -> Debug (via USB)\"; \"USART1 Bootloader (PB14/PB15)\" — FCC sheet, page 2"
        },
        {
          "source": "schematic",
          "quote": "U6 connects to NET0092 and NET0014 — Connections sheet, page 4; FCC2 labels PB15 as NET0092, PD8 as NET0014, and PB14 as NET0100 — FCC sheet, page 2"
        }
      ],
      "impact": "The USB-UART debug connection does not reach both pins of the specified USART1 interface, so UART debug or bootloader communication through U6 may fail.",
      "confidence": 0.82
    }
  ],
  "summary": "The FCC USB-UART bridge is routed to PB15 and PD8, while the schematic identifies PB14/PB15 as the USART1 bootloader pair and UART1 as the USB debug interface. This leaves PB14 disconnected from the bridge and substitutes a different MCU pin."
}

